WEBVTT

00:05.644 --> 00:07.612
Good morning, Charlie.

00:09.515 --> 00:11.073
Charlie?

00:18.090 --> 00:20.923
Good, I don't have to give him
mouth-to-mouth.

00:21.360 --> 00:23.157
- Morning.
Morning.

00:23.328 --> 00:26.491
- He's sleeping?
- Sure, let's call it sleep.

00:28.901 --> 00:32.735
Uncle Charlie, I'm gonna have a bowl
of Maple Loops, you want one?

00:44.149 --> 00:45.377
Are you sure he's okay?

00:45.551 --> 00:48.418
I never said he was okay.

00:55.527 --> 00:56.960
Freaky.

00:57.696 --> 01:00.756
You really shouldn't see him
like this, Jake.

01:07.506 --> 01:09.565
There, now you can
enjoy your breakfast.

01:10.342 --> 01:13.743
- What's wrong with him?
- Oh, he's getting old, kiddo.

01:14.012 --> 01:16.446
I wish you could've seen him
in his prime.

01:16.615 --> 01:17.843
He was like Babe Ruth.

01:18.350 --> 01:19.408
He played baseball?

01:19.585 --> 01:21.246
No, he was a drunken whoremonger.

01:23.155 --> 01:25.248
But there was none better.

01:27.126 --> 01:29.151
Oh, God, look what the cat dragged in.

01:29.328 --> 01:30.454
He didn't just drag it.

01:30.629 --> 01:33.826
He ate it, pooped it out
and then covered it with sand.

01:34.900 --> 01:36.367
You know what would be funny?

01:36.535 --> 01:38.264
To paint a big mustache on him.

01:39.938 --> 01:42.873
That would be hilarious, but no.

01:44.009 --> 01:45.476
Charlie?

01:46.512 --> 01:48.070
Charlie?

01:48.413 --> 01:50.142
Yeah?

01:50.449 --> 01:51.973
Are you okay?

01:52.151 --> 01:53.812
Yeah.

01:53.986 --> 01:56.079
What time did you get home?

01:56.522 --> 01:58.683
I'm home?

02:01.260 --> 02:02.852
You are.

02:03.729 --> 02:06.857
Oh, God, I'm blind.

02:12.371 --> 02:14.396
It's a miracle.

02:41.900 --> 02:43.663
Okay, see you tomorrow.

02:43.835 --> 02:45.427
Good night, Berta.

02:46.004 --> 02:47.062
Hey.

02:51.076 --> 02:53.067
Look who's finally up.

02:53.245 --> 02:54.269
How'd you sleep?

02:55.347 --> 02:57.281
Okay, I guess.

02:57.716 --> 02:59.684
Good, I'm glad.

03:03.222 --> 03:06.282
- Oh. Tater Tots.
- Help yourself.

03:08.961 --> 03:11.054
- Jake, I said no.
- I didn't do it.

03:11.230 --> 03:12.822
He didn't.

03:35.754 --> 03:37.187
What are you staring at?

03:37.623 --> 03:39.716
&lt;i>Nothing, señor.&lt;/i>

03:41.860 --> 03:43.828
So how are you feeling?

03:44.263 --> 03:46.857
That depends. What day is it?

03:48.033 --> 03:49.057
Saturday.

03:49.234 --> 03:52.169
Oh. Well, in that case, I feel great.

03:52.604 --> 03:53.662
Why in that case?

03:53.839 --> 03:56.603
If it was Thursday, I'd be a little worried.

03:57.042 --> 03:59.306
I don't know,
you've been pushing it hard lately.

03:59.478 --> 04:01.571
- What do you mean?
- You're not a kid anymore.

04:01.747 --> 04:02.873
Oh, please.

04:03.048 --> 04:04.515
I'm in the best shape of my life.

04:11.623 --> 04:13.955
Oh, that doesn't belong inside of me.

04:14.393 --> 04:17.521
It takes a lot to gross me out, but wow.

04:19.031 --> 04:21.727
Get your stuff together.
I'll bring you back to your mom's.

04:21.900 --> 04:23.094
Let me tell you something.

04:23.268 --> 04:25.702
You're only as young
as the women you feel.

04:27.572 --> 04:30.905
And lately, I've been feeling about 24.

04:31.510 --> 04:33.068
- Twenty-four?
- Yup.

04:33.245 --> 04:35.770
She doesn't think I'm old.
She thinks I'm cute and fun.

04:35.947 --> 04:37.642
- And rich.
- Yeah, the rich helps.

04:37.816 --> 04:39.443
I'm not that cute.

04:40.319 --> 04:44.312
Okay, fine. I understand the allure,
the nectar of the young berry.

04:46.625 --> 04:49.093
I know what happens
burning a candle at both ends.

04:49.494 --> 04:53.396
How would you know that? Did you take a
candle-making class at the Learning Annex?

04:53.932 --> 04:56.400
Hey, I have done my share
of walking on the wild side.

04:56.568 --> 04:57.967
The wild side?

04:58.570 --> 05:00.902
Okay, the rambunctious side.

05:01.239 --> 05:05.175
There comes a time in a mars life when
he has to start accepting his limitations.

05:05.344 --> 05:08.711
Yeah, well, my point is,
the day you start accepting limitations...

05:08.880 --> 05:10.677
...is the day you start dying.

05:11.983 --> 05:15.783
And I'm not dying, my friend,
I am living life to the fullest.

05:17.889 --> 05:21.347
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna go throw up and take a nap.

05:27.432 --> 05:28.865
That was fun.

05:30.869 --> 05:33.429
- Yeah.
- How long until you're ready to go again?

05:33.972 --> 05:35.667
You mean, tonight?

05:36.108 --> 05:37.439
Oh, yeah, I forgot.

05:37.609 --> 05:38.871
You're old.

05:39.044 --> 05:41.308
Hey, hey, hey, I'm not old.

05:41.480 --> 05:44.381
I'm just not a yogurt dispenser.

05:44.549 --> 05:46.449
You're almost as old as my dad.

05:47.152 --> 05:51.111
All right, listen, if you're looking to
go again, that's not the way to get there.

05:51.289 --> 05:53.382
Aw. Did I hurt your feelings?

05:53.558 --> 05:55.321
No, no, you didn't hurt my feelings.

05:55.494 --> 05:59.328
It's just there are certain biological
factors you have to take into account...

05:59.498 --> 06:01.523
Yeah, my dad takes viagra.

06:03.235 --> 06:04.930
Good for him.

06:06.171 --> 06:09.902
All I'm saying is, we could do something
else for a while and come back to this.

06:10.075 --> 06:12.600
- Great. Let's go to a club.
- Now?

06:12.778 --> 06:13.836
It's 11:00.

06:14.279 --> 06:16.144
So we'll get there early.

06:17.315 --> 06:19.579
Actually I was thinking
more along the lines...

06:19.751 --> 06:23.243
&lt;i>...of making some toaster pizzas
and watching The Daily Show.&lt;/i>

06:24.389 --> 06:25.981
- Oh.
- What?

06:27.092 --> 06:28.525
I'm bored.

06:28.693 --> 06:31.958
If we're not gonna have sex, you know,
I wanna go out.

06:32.397 --> 06:33.762
Okay, tell you what...

06:33.932 --> 06:37.663
...why don't you go out and,
you know, boogie oogie oogie?

06:38.370 --> 06:40.838
And when you come back,
wake me up and we'll have sex.

06:41.640 --> 06:43.437
That's a lame idea, Charlie.

06:43.608 --> 06:45.940
Okay, you can skip
the waking-me-up part.

06:46.111 --> 06:48.909
- I'm just gonna go call some friends.
- No, no, no, wait.

06:49.080 --> 06:50.206
Come here. Come here.

06:50.649 --> 06:52.173
I think I'm ready to go again.

06:52.617 --> 06:53.879
- Really?
- Really.

07:02.127 --> 07:03.594
I got nothing. Let's go dancing.

07:06.631 --> 07:09.395
Yeah, I'm coming with the guy
I told you about. The old guy.

07:11.603 --> 07:15.300
I don't know. I think he's got
a little brother who's old too.

07:16.575 --> 07:19.135
I'll ask him. Great, we'll see you there.

07:19.311 --> 07:20.972
Think your brother would wanna come?

07:21.413 --> 07:23.347
Alan? No, he's not the type.

07:23.515 --> 07:25.642
He'd be miserable going to a club
at this hour.

07:25.817 --> 07:27.580
Wait here. I'll go get him.

07:31.857 --> 07:33.449
- Hey.
- Oh, you just missed it.

07:33.625 --> 07:36.890
Jon Stewart made a very clever joke
about the budget deficit.

07:37.596 --> 07:39.894
Swell.
Get dressed. We're going dancing.

07:40.432 --> 07:42.400
Yeah, right. Toaster pizza?

07:42.567 --> 07:44.501
No. Come on. Let's go.

07:45.170 --> 07:46.637
- Are you serious?
- Yes.

07:46.805 --> 07:50.332
But it's after 11 and I'm all tucked in.

07:50.509 --> 07:53.535
- Too bad.
- I'm drinking Nighty-Night tea.

07:54.446 --> 07:57.904
Come on. Robin wants to go dancing
and I'm gonna need a designated driver.

07:58.149 --> 08:01.710
Hey, just because you're being a fool
trying to keep up with a 24-year-old girl...

08:01.887 --> 08:04.981
...doesn't mean I have to join you.
- She has a 24-year-old friend.

08:05.156 --> 08:07.181
Is it dressy-dressy or dressy-casual?

08:13.632 --> 08:15.691
Just take it. Maybe it'll loosen you up.

08:17.035 --> 08:18.059
I don't think so.

08:18.236 --> 08:21.637
Recent studies indicate that Ecstasy
may well deplete your spinal fluid.

08:22.374 --> 08:23.932
Yeah, so?

08:24.376 --> 08:26.435
So? Young lady, I am a chiropractor.

08:27.445 --> 08:29.003
Whoo.

08:29.881 --> 08:32.873
You know what?
My date isn't working out.

08:33.318 --> 08:36.446
Maybe you'd get somewhere
if you didn't talk to her like her father.

08:36.621 --> 08:40.523
Well, somebody has to because her real
father has obviously dropped the ball.

08:41.693 --> 08:43.786
Oh, wonderful, a smoker.

08:43.962 --> 08:48.626
So I guess you're counting on stem-cell
research to replace your spine and lungs.

08:51.169 --> 08:53.467
Alan, Alan, you're embarrassing me.

08:53.638 --> 08:55.629
Oh, I'm embarrassing you?
Look at yourself.

08:55.807 --> 08:59.538
You're standing in line in a dank alley
in the middle of the Urine District.

08:59.711 --> 09:02.202
Hey, hey, hey,
this is the hippest club in town.

09:02.380 --> 09:05.281
Oh, hip, schmip.
It's a toilet with a doorman.

09:07.586 --> 09:09.611
Somebody lit a doobie.

09:10.922 --> 09:13.891
Oh, yeah, oh, yeah.
That is definitely the ganja.

09:15.060 --> 09:17.051
Oh, great,
now we're all gonna get busted.

09:17.495 --> 09:20.328
Will you just relax
and let yourself have some fun?

09:20.498 --> 09:21.863
Oh, this is fun for you?

09:22.033 --> 09:23.933
Exhaust fumes and reefer smoke?

09:24.102 --> 09:26.036
Let me tell you something.
I am not a kid.

09:26.204 --> 09:29.537
I need plenty of rest, exercise
and a high-fiber diet and...

09:29.708 --> 09:31.835
oh, perfect, I just stepped on a condom.

09:33.578 --> 09:36.069
Go ahead. Have a good time.

09:36.281 --> 09:38.943
- Hold it.
- We're with them.

09:39.150 --> 09:41.243
- I don't think so.
- Oh, no, no. We are.

09:41.419 --> 09:45.515
Truth be told, I don't see a long-term
relationship in the offing. You understand.

09:45.690 --> 09:47.385
Don't touch the rope.

09:48.326 --> 09:49.452
Sorry.

09:49.628 --> 09:51.858
I didn't realize you were king of the rope.

09:53.031 --> 09:54.089
Shut up, Alan.

09:54.599 --> 09:56.692
You're not on the list,
you're not getting in.

09:56.868 --> 09:58.267
- You let the girls in.
- Alan...

09:58.436 --> 09:59.926
He let the girls in.

10:00.105 --> 10:02.903
That's because pretty girls
dress up the place.

10:03.074 --> 10:04.268
Watch how this works.

10:05.644 --> 10:10.138
Listen, why don't you check your list
for Jackson?

10:10.382 --> 10:12.543
Andrew Jackson.

10:14.753 --> 10:17.881
Nope. Got Tito and La Toya.

10:19.858 --> 10:21.416
Okay.

10:21.826 --> 10:24.124
What if I change my name to...

10:26.231 --> 10:28.165
...Ulysses S. Grant?

10:28.333 --> 10:31.097
You could change your name
to Condoleezza Rice.

10:32.070 --> 10:35.562
If you're not on the list and you're not
a celebrity, you're not getting in.

10:36.641 --> 10:40.270
All right, look, I didn't wanna have
to play this card but I'm Charlie Harper.

10:40.445 --> 10:42.242
I'm in the music business.

10:43.014 --> 10:44.675
I wrote the Maple Loops jingle.

10:46.451 --> 10:47.975
Granny's Big Fudge Nuggets?

10:48.553 --> 10:50.418
- Oh, I love those cookies.
- Great.

10:50.588 --> 10:52.078
- You got any on you?
- No.

10:52.257 --> 10:53.519
Beat it.

10:54.426 --> 10:56.826
Charlie, Charlie, let me handle this.

10:57.462 --> 10:58.895
Sir...

11:01.099 --> 11:03.226
...I am Matthew Broderick.

11:03.902 --> 11:04.960
Who?

11:05.670 --> 11:07.501
Bruno, they're with me.

11:07.672 --> 11:10.698
Are you sure?
This is a good chance to cut them loose.

11:10.875 --> 11:12.502
Guys, come on.

11:18.283 --> 11:22.117
Matthew Broderick is a gifted actor
and the toast of Broadway.

11:28.493 --> 11:31.121
Oh, for God's sake,
will you stop complaining?

11:31.296 --> 11:34.629
Well, I'm sorry, but the music in that club
was so loud, my ears are still ringing.

11:38.837 --> 11:42.466
You know what that sound is? That is
the sound of the hairs in my ear dying.

11:46.077 --> 11:48.136
I am talking permanent hearing loss,
Charlie.

11:48.313 --> 11:49.780
Those little hairs don't grow back.

11:51.916 --> 11:54.077
Oh, wait. Let's see something.

12:00.125 --> 12:02.821
C- sharp.

12:02.994 --> 12:06.896
C- sharp is the sound
of encroaching deafness.

12:07.365 --> 12:09.424
Listen to you. You're like an old man.

12:09.601 --> 12:11.694
I can't listen to me. All I hear is:

12:15.273 --> 12:17.298
Worst night of my life.

12:17.742 --> 12:20.370
You're just ticked off
because you couldn't keep up.

12:20.545 --> 12:21.569
I couldn't keep up?

12:21.746 --> 12:25.546
I was out on the dance floor with the girls,
while you were sleeping in the booth.

12:25.884 --> 12:27.511
I wasrt sleeping.

12:27.685 --> 12:31.086
I was closing my eyes because
I couldn't bear to watch you do this:

12:35.660 --> 12:36.684
I was voguing.

12:38.830 --> 12:41.196
You were napping.

12:41.366 --> 12:43.425
Nobody vogues anymore, Alan.

12:43.601 --> 12:47.435
And guess what,
nobody does the robot anymore either.

12:49.174 --> 12:51.642
Oh, yeah? Then why
did it catch on with the others?

12:51.810 --> 12:55.143
It didn't catch on.
They were openly mocking you.

12:56.080 --> 12:57.240
What do you want from me?

12:57.415 --> 12:59.747
I went to the club.
I went to the after-hours club.

12:59.918 --> 13:01.010
I went out to breakfast.

13:01.186 --> 13:04.952
I held my date's hair while she vomited
pancakes in the parking lot.

13:05.623 --> 13:07.921
If you werert whining
about wanting to go home...

13:08.092 --> 13:10.117
...you'd be having sex with her
right now.

13:10.295 --> 13:14.129
Oh, darn. What man doesn't dream
of kissing secondhand pancakes?

13:16.301 --> 13:18.132
And I have to go to work.

13:18.303 --> 13:21.295
You know what? You are a fuddy-duddy.

13:21.472 --> 13:23.303
I'm...? I'm a fuddy-duddy?

13:23.474 --> 13:26.068
Hey, if the orthopedic shoe fits, wear it.

13:27.445 --> 13:28.537
They are not orthopedic.

13:28.713 --> 13:31.978
They merely have a reinforced arch
for the active lifestyle.

13:33.685 --> 13:35.243
And you were napping.

13:35.420 --> 13:37.479
Okay, maybe I needed a little shuteye.

13:37.655 --> 13:41.022
But that's only because
I had vigorous sex earlier.

13:41.459 --> 13:44.656
Oh, let's face it.
We're both too old for the MTv lifestyle.

13:44.829 --> 13:47.889
MTv? Did they just defrost you?

13:49.834 --> 13:53.361
Okay. MTv, vH1,
whatever the kids are watching.

13:53.538 --> 13:56.939
My point is,
I am comfortable acting my age...

13:57.108 --> 13:58.666
...while you are in deep denial.

13:58.843 --> 14:01.607
Hey, hey,
I am not in denial about anything.

14:01.779 --> 14:04.680
I am a young, vibrant man
in the prime of my life. I'm...

14:12.724 --> 14:13.952
What?

14:14.125 --> 14:16.389
Young people have phlegm too.

14:17.295 --> 14:18.557
Sure.

14:18.730 --> 14:21.130
Anyway, as I was...

14:23.501 --> 14:24.525
oh, God.

14:25.603 --> 14:27.127
What's the matter?

14:27.405 --> 14:28.599
My chest.

14:29.007 --> 14:30.998
Are you okay?

14:31.342 --> 14:32.934
I don't know.

14:33.544 --> 14:35.205
- Hey, Alan?
- Yeah.

14:36.814 --> 14:39.806
Do you think it's too late
to start jogging?

14:41.986 --> 14:45.547
Damn it, what kind of hospital
is this? Where the hell are the doctors?

14:45.723 --> 14:46.985
That's my brother in there.

14:47.158 --> 14:48.887
If he dies, I'm homeless.

14:55.266 --> 14:56.733
Uh, everything's fine.

14:57.769 --> 15:00.932
Uh, they're just gonna run some tests.
Not to worry.

15:01.105 --> 15:03.039
Easy for you to say.

15:03.641 --> 15:05.336
Listen, Alan.

15:05.510 --> 15:08.104
If I don't make it,
you need to know about my will.

15:08.279 --> 15:11.442
Hey, I don't wanna hear that kind of talk.
You're gonna make it.

15:13.351 --> 15:16.115
But go on. Finish what you were saying.

15:17.622 --> 15:20.921
First of all,
I left the house to you and Jake.

15:21.092 --> 15:22.491
Yes!

15:25.663 --> 15:27.563
You're gonna make it.

15:29.734 --> 15:32.498
Just so you know,
there's two mortgages on it...

15:32.670 --> 15:35.537
...and the property taxes
are $50,000 a year.

15:36.774 --> 15:38.605
Uh, 50,000?

15:42.513 --> 15:44.037
Uh, excuse me.

15:47.919 --> 15:50.479
Do you gotta flatline
to get a little help around here?

15:52.457 --> 15:56.154
Do you gotta move to Canada
to get some decent medical care?

15:57.762 --> 15:59.320
Uh, they'll be right here.

16:00.231 --> 16:02.995
So 50 grand, huh?

16:03.434 --> 16:06.892
Boy, I don't know
how I could afford that.

16:07.071 --> 16:09.039
You know,
unless I came into some money.

16:09.207 --> 16:12.142
You know, an ineritance or something.

16:12.310 --> 16:13.470
There's no money, Alan.

16:14.145 --> 16:15.169
None?

16:15.346 --> 16:17.405
The whole thing's a house of cards.

16:19.484 --> 16:20.883
Huh.

16:26.357 --> 16:28.848
Okay, I did not wanna have to do this...

16:29.027 --> 16:30.722
...but I am Matthew Broderick.

16:31.996 --> 16:33.987
And that is my brother lying there.

16:34.165 --> 16:36.258
I am so sorry, Mr. Broderick.

16:36.434 --> 16:38.493
&lt;i>- I loved you in The Producers.
Thank you.&lt;/i>

16:40.204 --> 16:43.264
Okay, let's have a look-see, huh?

16:44.842 --> 16:48.403
According to your tests, you just had
an acute attack of indigestion.

16:50.882 --> 16:52.679
- It was gas?
- Yes. A big bubble.

16:52.850 --> 16:54.943
About the size of a pomegranate.

16:55.453 --> 16:57.114
What have you had to eat recently?

16:57.655 --> 16:58.679
Nothing much.

16:58.856 --> 17:01.825
He had Belgian waffles,
link sausages, two Red Bulls...

17:01.993 --> 17:04.791
...a quart of Scotch
and the tongue of a 24-year-old actress.

17:05.229 --> 17:06.719
He asked what I ate, Alan.

17:07.165 --> 17:08.723
And I told him, Charlie.

17:10.034 --> 17:12.594
Oh-ho, you're a dirty bird.

17:13.771 --> 17:17.730
Well, the good news is that you are
a perfectly healthy 50-year-old man.

17:18.509 --> 17:19.533
I'm only 40.

17:19.977 --> 17:21.706
Tell that to your liver.

17:23.548 --> 17:25.311
I would recommend you slow down a bit.

17:25.483 --> 17:28.111
- I've been saying the same thing.
- And you.

17:28.286 --> 17:31.153
&lt;i>Why no sequel to Ferris Bueller, huh?&lt;/i>

17:31.322 --> 17:33.222
I wait and I wait.

17:33.658 --> 17:35.285
I'm sorry, I'll get on it.

17:35.460 --> 17:38.156
Ah, give the people what they want.

17:43.000 --> 17:44.991
So gas.

17:47.071 --> 17:48.402
Good news, huh?

17:48.573 --> 17:52.475
- A little embarrassing, but yeah.
- What are you embarrassed about?

17:52.910 --> 17:56.107
I don't know.
The paramedics, the ambulance...

17:56.280 --> 17:59.772
...the crying and the last-minute
negotiations with God.

17:59.951 --> 18:03.148
Oh, right. Are you still planning
on teaching piano to orphans?

18:03.321 --> 18:05.585
If any show up, sure.

18:06.390 --> 18:10.554
All right. Well, will you at least accept
the fact that you have to slow down?

18:11.229 --> 18:13.493
Yeah. Yeah.

18:14.365 --> 18:16.492
It's weird, Alan.

18:17.201 --> 18:20.034
It seems like just yesterday, I could...

18:20.204 --> 18:23.935
I could party all night,
eat and drink anything I wanted to.

18:24.108 --> 18:26.008
Now a couple of Red Bulls and a waffle...

18:26.177 --> 18:29.476
...and I'm sitting in the emergency room
praying for a fart.

18:33.751 --> 18:36.777
Now you know why I ordered
tomato juice and cottage cheese.

18:38.289 --> 18:41.224
- I admit, you take good care of yourself.
- I try.

18:42.059 --> 18:43.856
I guess that's why I keep you around.

18:44.028 --> 18:45.393
Because I'm a good example?

18:45.563 --> 18:48.327
No, you clod, spare parts.

18:52.970 --> 18:54.301
What are we watching?

18:54.839 --> 18:56.966
&lt;i>Antiques Roadshow.&lt;/i>

18:57.642 --> 19:00.543
This woman thinks she has
Martha Washingtors butter churn.

19:02.213 --> 19:03.646
Huh.

19:03.814 --> 19:05.338
Toaster pizza?

19:05.516 --> 19:06.983
Thank you.

19:07.451 --> 19:10.147
- So are you going out tonight?
- Ah, what's the point?

19:11.789 --> 19:14.189
Look, Charlie,
I'm glad you're slowing down a bit...

19:14.358 --> 19:17.122
...but you haven't been out of the house
in a week.

19:17.295 --> 19:19.058
Ah, it's too depressing.

19:19.230 --> 19:21.425
Wherever I go,
I'm the oldest guy in the room.

19:22.800 --> 19:24.495
Even here.

19:28.906 --> 19:31.431
Hey, what would you think
about getting a cat?

19:33.177 --> 19:35.042
Okay, that's it. Put some clothes on.

19:35.213 --> 19:36.305
We're going out.

19:36.480 --> 19:37.504
It's 9:00.

19:37.682 --> 19:39.445
I was gonna make some kettle corn.

19:39.951 --> 19:41.851
Forget the corn. You're coming with me.

19:42.019 --> 19:44.487
- Where are we going?
- You'll see.

19:45.856 --> 19:47.414
Can you drive?

19:47.592 --> 19:49.958
I don't like to drive at night.

19:52.697 --> 19:53.994
What the hell is this place?

19:54.165 --> 19:56.326
- The fountain of youth.
- What?

19:56.500 --> 19:57.558
Follow me.

20:02.640 --> 20:06.201
Ooh, look, young stuff.

20:07.912 --> 20:11.245
Alan, you're a genius.

20:17.421 --> 20:20.754
- May I ask you a personal question?
- Sure.

20:21.192 --> 20:22.489
How old are you?

20:22.660 --> 20:23.854
I just turned 40.

20:24.028 --> 20:27.020
Ah! You're a baby.

20:27.698 --> 20:30.599
Well, yeah.

20:32.270 --> 20:33.999
Hey, I have a little riddle for you.

20:34.171 --> 20:35.229
All right.

20:35.406 --> 20:39.103
What has multiple orgasms and hums?

20:39.644 --> 20:40.736
I give up.

20:46.517 --> 20:48.212
Oh.

20:49.720 --> 20:51.085
Come on, I'll show you.

20:53.891 --> 20:56.189
Alan? Alan, I'm leaving.

20:58.763 --> 21:00.196
And may God bless you.
